nc-reagent-name-trauma-analgesic = trauma analgesic
nc-reagent-desc-trauma-analgesic = Suppresses pain perception without repairing the underlying injury.
nc-reagent-name-surgical-anesthetic = surgical anesthetic
nc-reagent-desc-surgical-anesthetic = Produces controlled anesthesia; excessive concentration depresses respiration.
nc-reagent-name-sedative = clinical sedative
nc-reagent-desc-sedative = Reduces awareness and movement while leaving traumatic damage unchanged.
nc-reagent-name-vasopressor = vasopressor
nc-reagent-desc-vasopressor = Supports cardiac output and vascular tone during resuscitation.
nc-reagent-name-antiarrhythmic = antiarrhythmic
nc-reagent-desc-antiarrhythmic = Stabilizes an unstable rhythm but cannot restart an arrested heart.
nc-reagent-name-respiratory-stimulant = respiratory stimulant
nc-reagent-desc-respiratory-stimulant = Improves the output of functioning lungs; it cannot replace absent lungs.
nc-reagent-name-broad-antibiotic = broad-spectrum antibiotic
nc-reagent-desc-broad-antibiotic = Suppresses susceptible wound infection while therapeutic concentration is maintained.
nc-reagent-name-antitoxin = systemic antitoxin
nc-reagent-desc-antitoxin = Accelerates clearance of circulating toxic burden through functioning organs.
nc-reagent-name-immunosuppressant = immunosuppressant
nc-reagent-desc-immunosuppressant = Suppresses transplant rejection while increasing vulnerability to infection.
nc-reagent-name-procoagulant = procoagulant
nc-reagent-desc-procoagulant = Reduces active bleeding through systemic clot support; it does not close a wound.
nc-reagent-name-stimulant = clinical stimulant
nc-reagent-desc-stimulant = Improves arousal and cardiopulmonary drive; overdose destabilizes physiology.
nc-reagent-name-anticoagulant = anticoagulant
nc-reagent-desc-anticoagulant = Reduces clot formation and increases bleeding while its concentration remains therapeutic.
nc-reagent-name-vasodilator = vasodilator
nc-reagent-desc-vasodilator = Reduces vascular tone; unsafe dosing can collapse perfusion.
nc-reagent-name-synthetic-oxygen-carrier = synthetic oxygen carrier
nc-reagent-desc-synthetic-oxygen-carrier = Temporarily adds oxygen-carrying capacity to circulating fluid without replacing lost blood volume.
nc-reagent-name-cyberware-coolant-agent = cyberware coolant agent
nc-reagent-desc-cyberware-coolant-agent = Circulates through compatible implants and removes measured excess heat; it does not repair organic tissue.

